 "literal": "Well-investigated long erect matted hair / ancient lord's mouth not leaving / one-desired two-times-two's / six-understood one ancient book / enmity saw-ones superiority to subdue / truth-like falsehood having understood / falsehood not considering truth having established / twenty-one departments without obstacle completed / repute-abundant excellence's strong-ones descendant / for the ritual desiring you wore / forest deer's buck skin / shoulder sacred thread upon to shine / evil shunned rare chastity's / virtue praised bangle having worn / small forehead great wide hip / few words abundant hair your / status-suited your equal wives / to themselves assigned duties to perform / forest or country saying there / fourteen places without failing / water to be ashamed ghee distributing / number to be ashamed many sacrificing / earth to be ashamed fame spreading / rare sacred great time / guests received your perfected eminent state / always may we see indeed oh we in the west / gold-yielding long mountain cloud thunder if roars / flower-blooming fresh water Kaveri protects / cool water garden our village there / eating and eating and riding and let us play / I will go indeed oh without departing / clouds to reach extended long mountain's / bamboo-growing Himalayas like / may you stand indeed you upon the earth",
 "translation": "O descendant of wise men of abundant repute and excellence! You who, for the sake of sacred rituals, wear the skin of a forest buck so that it shines upon the sacred thread on your shoulder, following the ancient book of six parts and four Vedas established by the matted-haired Lord Shiva. Your chaste wives, wearing bangles praised by virtue, perform their assigned duties. Without failing in any of the fourteen worlds, you distribute ghee so abundantly that water is ashamed, perform so many sacrifices that numbers are ashamed, and spread your fame so wide that the earth is ashamed. May we always see your eminent state of receiving guests in the sacred morning. We shall now return to our village in the west, nourished by the Kaveri river with fresh blooming flowers, where we shall eat, drink, ride, and rejoice. I shall depart now. May you live long on this earth, without departing, like the bamboo-growing Himalayas whose high peaks reach the clouds!",
